From 9a0e9afa40dfe7d301e971f82337310aec02d960 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:30:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): kernel creates the fresh in-scope resume
 requester for a continuation_exhausted park [daveey]

The supervisor resume op needs a requester within 3 creator hops of the target AND created after
its current park. A parked card cannot create one and every older card predates the park, so no
card could ever pass both fences (layers t_01a19084a3b36956). Each dispatcher tick now creates
one recovery card per resumable continuation_exhausted park (creator_task_id=target,
created_by=kanban-recovery, idempotency key recovery:<target>:<park event id>). All resume fences
are unchanged. No card for human-gated, non-exhausted, budget-spent or recovery cards; the stale
triage sweep waits while the park's recovery card is open.
---
